==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Salvation's Daughter Lunacia''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Between her lack of [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] and exceedingly low range, Luna often finds herself stuck between a rock and a hard place. She sees her best usage in situations that encourage the use of cheap, spammable attackers to accumulate consistent damage, specifically against enemies that don't already outrange her like [[One Horn]] and [[Bore]] variants. Her [[Freeze]]'s activation rate and uptime are quite awful, so consider it a bonus alongside her [[Explosion]].

Where Luna really shines is mainly against Zombies, as she outranges many of the basic peons like [[Zang Roo]], [[Zory]], [[Zuche]], or [[Zigge]], and can catch them by surprise as they're unburrowing. A swarm of Lunas can absolutely shred through melee enemies with their ~6,000 DPS on average, not even mentioning the fact that each one comes bundled in with passable crowd-control and pierce. Despite being outperformed in most aspects by her Evolved Form, Luna still shouldn't be discounted whenever you need a stackable rusher.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Salvation's Daughter Lunacia differs from other [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] units primarily in her target traits. Being limited to [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]], [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]], [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]], and [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]], Lunacia exchanges generalist value for complete specialist obliteration.

Her crowd-control is absolutely ridiculous; creating Explosions that are guaranteed to Freeze all targets within an effective 675 range, all the while retaining a ~40% uptime. Such a level of performance matches and surpasses many dedicated specialists for these traits, to the point where she can completely supersede the role of a controller entirely. This isn't even mentioning the fact that her damage output is equally as powerful. To put things into perspective: a [[Fruit Treasures|Fruited]] target hit by the full brunt of her Omni Strike and Explosion will take 64,000 damage per attack cycle, which translates to just over 12,000 DPS (the same as [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli, Daughter of Chaos']] at equal levels, all while having double her effective HP).

[[Wave Shield]] gives Lunacia an entirely different niche to operate within, and thus completely dominate. Having such a wide array of targets makes her a strong options for most Wave enemies, from [[Youcan]] to [[Masked Grandmaster Cat (Enemy)|Masked Grandmaster Cat]]. Furthermore, she's one of the only backline Wave Shields in the game, giving her far better survivability over options like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] or [[EVA Unit-00 (Uber Rare Cat)|Eva Unit-00]].

All in all, Lunacia is a fantastic unit with viability at all stages of the game. Explosions aren't resisted by very many enemies, so there's hardly a situation where her abilities can't be fully utilized to their maximum potential. In spite of her lack of relevant resistances, besides [[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]], most enemies will find it nigh-impossible to break through her.

