==Trivia==
*Luna is the name of the [[wikipedia:Luna (goddess)|Roman Moon goddess]].
*Lunacia's Japanese name and description refer to her as a 天女 ''[https://yokai.com/tennyo/ tennyo]'' (lit. "heavenly woman"), a specifically female ''[[wikipedia:Tennin|tennin]]'' in Japanese Buddhism, originating from Hindu and Buddhist mythology as heavenly female water nymphs called [[wikipedia:Apsara|apsaras]]. ''Tennin'' are beautiful, angel-like beings who reside in the Buddhist realm of heaven Tendō (possibly the "foreign land" in her Japanese description) as companions of Buddhas and Bodhisattvas, and as such are associated with lotus flowers.
**The lotuses in her design and mention of fate in her Japanese description suggest that she may also be based on the Hindu goddess [[wikipedia:Lakshimi|Lakshimi]], whose name means "she who leads to one's goal".
*Luna's pose is similar to [[wikipedia: DreamWorks Animation|DreamWorks Animation]]'s mascot, the [[wikia:dreamworks:Moon Child|Moon Child]].
*[[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Squire Luno]] is a counterpart to Luna:
**The names Luno and Luna are only one letter apart.
**Luno and Luna have the same moon symbols across their forms.
**Their Japanese descriptions both say that they do not know their own mission.
**Both have Omni Strike, immunity to Curse and [[Special Abilities|abilities]] that target four traits, including [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]].
*The "sha" in Lunacia's romanized Japanese name, Runāsha (ルナーシャ), may be derived from ''[[wikipedia:Yaksha|yaksha]]'', ''[[wikipedia:Ganesha|Ganesha]]'' or 釈迦 ''Shaka'' ([[wikipedia:Gautama Buddha|Gautama Buddha]]).
*Lunacia's Japanese description is similar to the Phonos in how it focuses on fate: [[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]] shattered their own fate, [[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]] severs the cycle of fate, and Lunacia brings peace to Cats trapped by their fate. However, they use different words for fate: Lunacia uses 宿命 ''shukumei'' (one's predetermined fate) whereas the Phonos use 運命 ''unmei'' (can also be translated as "fate", but has more to do with luck and fortune and is technically changeable, unlike the fate decided before one's birth).
*Lunacia appears to be doing the "As above, so below" pose in her walking animation.
*Lunacia's attack animation somewhat resembles that of [[Kamukura (Uber Rare Cat)|Kamukura]], both charging up before releasing a large beam of sorts (a stream of water in Kamukura's case) that bursts from the ground, causing a splash of water.
*She is the first [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]]-exclusive unit with abilities that do not target all traits.
*Lunacia is one of the units to have had their description rewritten in [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]], as "Also blocks Wave attacks" was changed to "plus Wave Shield".

